import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'two-phase':('Morgoth-depth pass leaves a stale skip entry','At depth 100 the Borg first evaluates its special Morgoth-depth Teleport Other, which stores the same monster twice (Morgoth assumed present and little mana left). The regular Teleport Other evaluation then targets the kobold: the original also suppresses the hill giant left over in the second slot, valuing the cast at the kobold plus the giant instead of the kobold alone. The fix stops at the listed entries, so the value is one candidate\'s list.'),
 'no-morgoth-phase':('Control: no deep pass, no phantom','Without the Morgoth-depth evaluation the second slot is never written. Both versions value the cast at the hill giant\'s danger, and the logs are identical before and after the fix.'),
 'single':('Control: a stale self-entry is harmless','Only the kobold exists, so the deep pass stores the kobold in both slots. When the regular evaluation later reads one slot past its list, it finds the kobold itself: a duplicate, not a phantom. Both versions value the cast identically.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw}
  for tag,key in (('MORGOTH','morgoth'),('OUTCOME','outcome')):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r' (.*)',raw)
   entry[key]={k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',match[1])} if match else None
  entry['kills']=[{k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',l)} for l in raw.splitlines() if l.startswith('KILL ')]
  entry['passed']='native-c/CBUG-0051 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Teleport Other skips only the monsters it lists</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native Teleport Other evaluations at depth 100</p><h1>The Teleport Other skip list reads one entry too far</h1><p>A level-30 Mage considers Teleport Other on depth 100 with a kobold beside it and a hill giant to the other side. The Borg\'s Morgoth-depth pass stores the giant in the second slot of its skip list; the regular evaluation then targets the kobold, and the original danger check walks one entry past the list and also suppresses that leftover giant. The cast is valued as if it removed both monsters.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><br><button data-step="0">Danger of each monster</button><button data-step="1">Morgoth-depth pass</button><button data-step="2">Regular evaluation</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the controls establish</h2><p>Without the Morgoth-depth pass the second slot is never written and both versions agree. When only one monster exists, the leftover slot holds that same monster, so a duplicate is harmless. Only the two-monster sequence with the deep pass first changes the value.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Mage level 31, depth 100, seed 1000, lit constructed arena, Teleport Other known, full mana for the regular evaluation and 30 mana during the Morgoth-depth pass. The Borg\'s own depth-100 assumption that Morgoth is present is set directly, matching what borg-update.c derives there. The production launch calls from both Teleport Other defenses are used unchanged; the target-candidate list is filled the same way the defense fills it.</p><p>This isolates the skip-list read, not full autonomous play or monster AI casting. Danger figures are the Borg\'s heuristic, not HP predictions. No death or survival claim.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/67">CBUG-0051 / issue67</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;let step=2;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);let ks=d.kills||[];p.querySelector('.num').textContent=step===0?ks.map(k=>`#${k.index}: ${k.danger}`).join('  '):step===1?(d.morgoth?`Slots after the deep pass: ${d.morgoth.slot0}, ${d.morgoth.slot1}`:'No deep pass in this control'):`Cast valued at ${d.outcome?d.outcome.p2:'n/a'}`;p.querySelector('.state').textContent=step===0?'Danger of each listed monster.':step===1?(d.morgoth?'Both slots hold the same monster index.':'The second slot is never written.'):'Value of the winning target candidate.';p.querySelector('.action').textContent=step===2?(d.passed?'Only the listed monster is skipped.':'One slot too far is also skipped: the value includes a monster the cast does not remove.'):'';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}let a=c.before.outcome,b=c.after.outcome;document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='two-phase'?`Original values the cast at ${a.p2} (kobold 16 plus leftover giant 128); the correction at ${b.p2} (the winning candidate's own list).`:'Both versions value the cast identically in this control; the logs match byte for byte.';for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.classList.toggle('active',Number(b.dataset.step)===step)}select.addEventListener('change',()=>{step=2;draw()});for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{step=Number(b.dataset.step);draw()});draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
